From: Joel Gerber <Jitsusama@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ipc: report tiled windows' positions in the workspace view

WindowLayout::tile_pos_in_workspace_view was only filled for floating
windows, so a client placing something over a tiled window, such as a
notification kept inside the window under it, couldn't tell where that
window was.

Tiled windows now report it too, taken where the view comes to rest
rather than where it's drawn this frame, and without column or tile
render offsets, so an animation or a gesture in progress sends no layout
change on every frame: the position changes once, when the target does.

A client riding a tile's edge as it moves has to follow the animation
itself, so a tiled window's layout also says which animation moving or
resizing its tile began last (WindowLayout::tile_animation: Resize,
TileMove, ColumnMove, ViewMove or WorkspaceSlide) and how many real
milliseconds before the layout went out it began
(tile_animation_began_ms_ago). A layout goes out again when another
animation begins, never as one runs on or ends, so the report still
changes once per change rather than once a frame.

---
diff --git a/niri-ipc/src/lib.rs b/niri-ipc/src/lib.rs
index 0aa3cb4..84e72c8 100644
--- a/niri-ipc/src/lib.rs
+++ b/niri-ipc/src/lib.rs
@@ -1383,6 +1383,9 @@ pub struct WindowLayout {
     /// Tile position within the current view of the workspace.
     ///
     /// This is the same "workspace view" as in gradients' `relative-to` in the niri config.
+    ///
+    /// For tiled windows, this is where the tile sits once the view comes to rest: it does not
+    /// follow view or tile animations, and changes when their targets change.
     pub tile_pos_in_workspace_view: Option<(f64, f64)>,
     /// Location of the window's visual geometry within its tile.
     ///
@@ -1390,6 +1393,37 @@ pub struct WindowLayout {
     /// the distance from the corner of the black backdrop to the corner of the (centered) window
     /// contents.
     pub window_offset_in_tile: (f64, f64),
+    /// The animation moving or resizing the tile that began last, while it runs.
+    ///
+    /// Only tiled windows say it. It's `None` when nothing moves the tile, and when what moves
+    /// it follows a gesture, which has no beginning to say.
+    pub tile_animation: Option<TileAnimation>,
+    /// How many milliseconds before this layout was sent its `tile_animation` began, in real
+    /// time, whatever the animations' slowdown.
+    ///
+    /// A layout is sent again when an animation begins, but not as this grows or as the
+    /// animation ends; the next layout sent carries it as of then. A layout niri answers a
+    /// request with, rather than sends in the event stream, says it as of when that layout was
+    /// last sent.
+    pub tile_animation_began_ms_ago: Option<f64>,
+}
+
+/// What moves or resizes a tile, as [`WindowLayout::tile_animation`] says.
+#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
+#[cfg_attr(feature = "json-schema", derive(schemars::JsonSchema))]
+pub enum TileAnimation {
+    /// The window resizing, on the `window-resize` animation.
+    Resize,
+    /// The tile moving within its column or between columns, on `window-movement`.
+    TileMove,
+    /// The tile's column moving as one beside it opens, closes or resizes, on
+    /// `window-movement`, or on `window-resize` when it's a resize that moves it.
+    ColumnMove,
+    /// The workspace's view scrolling across its columns, on `horizontal-view-movement`, or on
+    /// `window-resize` when it's a resize that scrolls it.
+    ViewMove,
+    /// The monitor sliding between its workspaces, on `workspace-switch`.
+    WorkspaceSlide,
 }
 
